candidates.G2_headroom:
FAILS (exploratory, spent data, unreviewed): no headroom, the same pattern as screen #2. Setup: 257 groups with at least 100 trips on both the fit days (14-17 Sep) and the evaluation days (18-24 Sep); 265,977 evaluation trips. Width of the 80% interval [q10, q90] per arm:
- fixed per group, fitted on 14-17 Sep and transferred: 35.3 s (upper miss 10.3%);
- hindsight constant per group: 35.9 s;
- hindsight per time band: 35.6 s;
- hindsight per day and time band (a time-varying oracle): 35.2 s;
- online ACI tracker: 36.4 s (misses 10.0% / 9.8%);
- rolling window of the last 30 trips: 34.0 s, but its upper miss rises to 12.5%.
The best time-varying hindsight is only 1.9% narrower than the hindsight constant, and the transferred fixed margin is already narrower (-1.4%). In the green-throughout subset (170 groups, 111,082 trips) the fixed margin is 9.6 s and the day-and-band hindsight 9.8 s. Why it could have differed from screen #2: here the uncertainty comes from traffic (dwell times, queues), not from the signal program. The data still show per-group quantiles that transfer from week to week. Any remaining gain is in better point ETAs (a prediction problem, already worked on by vendors), not in the margin. Integer-second ties make lower-tail misses fall below 10%.

